### Performance against the base

The base revision and this change, each booted 5 times in turn in one VM job. Boot times and idle RAM compare the best of the 5 boots of each side; running services and the benchmarks run after each boot (CPU, memory bandwidth, disk) their median; the closure that of the real system. A metric is flagged only past both its relative and its absolute threshold, a benchmark when it drops. The benchmark thresholds come from the noise of local runs and a shared CI runner is noisier: read their trend over several runs, not one value. Informational: it never blocks the merge.

No metric crossed its threshold.

#### example

| Metric | Base | This change | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Boot, total (best) | n/a | 7.0 s | n/a |
| Boot, userspace (best) | n/a | 3.0 s | n/a |
| Idle RAM (best) | n/a | 400.0 MiB | n/a |
| Closure | n/a | 2048.0 MiB | n/a |
| Running services (median) | n/a | 20 | n/a |
| CPU, sysbench (median) | n/a | 7500.0 events/s | n/a |
| Memory bandwidth, sysbench (median) | n/a | 50000.0 MiB/s | n/a |
| Disk, 4k random read (median) | n/a | 50000 IOPS | n/a |
